WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 056. A LIST OF ASSETS IS NOT A MOAT. Data, rights, relationships, workflows, trust, knowledge, and feedback may matter—but possession or access does not establish ownership, control, or durable advantage.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
MAP THE TOPOLOGY. ASSET · RIGHT · RELATIONSHIP · DEPENDENCY. Use an exact-bound synthetic organization. Connect each claimed asset to source, permission, control, replaceability, transfer limits, upkeep, evidence, and dependent capabilities.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
DISTINGUISH THE CLAIM. POSSESS · ACCESS · PERMISSION · CONTROL. Keep legal ownership separate from holding a copy, reaching a resource, receiving limited permission, or controlling a workflow. Name expiry, revocation, and uncertainty.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
REMOVE A SUPPOSED MOAT. WATCH THE TOPOLOGY CHANGE. Delete one illustrative node or edge and recompute only declared dependencies, substitutes, feedback paths, concentration, fragility, and what remains unsupported.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. A MAP IS NOT A VERDICT. The demo cannot determine title, ownership, IP rights, legality, valuation, investability, competitive advantage, durability, defensibility, or commercial success.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. TEST WHAT SURVIVES REMOVAL. DEFENSIBILITY BECOMES LEGIBLE WHEN CLAIMED ASSETS, RIGHTS, DEPENDENCIES, SUBSTITUTES, EVIDENCE, AND FAILURE PATHS CAN BE READ TOGETHER.

